<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aster Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aster Revolution was the uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> of 28-31 October 1918, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> collapsed at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Soldiers and civilians wearing asters as their emblem forced the appointment of Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi">Mihály Károlyi</a> as prime minister on 31 October, the day former premier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istvan-tisza">István Tisza</a> was murdered. It led to the proclamation of the Hungarian Democratic Republic in November.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aster-revolution.jpg" alt="Aster Revolution" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mazarin07 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:800px-Oszirozsas_forradalmarok.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
